{"id": "EUVD-2026-76530", "enisaUuid": "a7266385-c37b-3845-8a44-a8a283567bd9", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\neventfs: Initialize ei->children and ei->list in init_ei()\n\neventfs_create_dir() allocates the eventfs_inode and initializes it with\ninit_ei(). But this does not initialize the eventfs_inode list_heads. If\nthe eventfs_create_dir() fails due to memory pressure, it will call\nfree_ei() before it initialized the lists, and that checks to make sure\nthe eventfs_inode has no children. But because the list wasn't\ninitialized, it will give a false warning.\n\nFix it by moving the list initialization into init_ei().\n\n[ Rewrote change log ]", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:45:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:49:50", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/069729282fbecfaa8a54062266c338ed23f08005", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c480f8af173d5b19c6d9c4311df6bbe352face9e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5333e18e6b425fcc39c7fea89e3949a2a98bc5e4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/76e0f85f650738d768449dbccbc7c55d05f5b609", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1704aaaf5d22bc765c168402350d191e24e245bc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89618", "GHSA-jw9q-gp66-86rq"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "03a4f36a-877c-3a89-bd11-dfec213b7555", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.18 <6.6.157"}, {"id": "1cff4a45-684c-3544-8d53-92f259af3370", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5790b1fb3d672d9a1fe3881a7181dfdbe741568f <76e0f85f650738d768449dbccbc7c55d05f5b609"}, {"id": "30b763c4-72fd-3afc-819b-e9909985ca16", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "36384d3a-29da-371e-ac16-a2d019b9fd61", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "3e5a881e-42b5-3faf-9de1-7e3791172be7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "7b8454bc-b3ba-355f-8ac7-dfd1ef622aa4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "840b11b9-a747-3f22-a32e-cdf52f8dd1fd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "35ee34c0f6d578c9d245438ca29bf2e7024a5a65 <069729282fbecfaa8a54062266c338ed23f08005"}, {"id": "8dde4fbc-9d03-307f-9d11-c91ca68ecc4e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "ba478ee2-dac6-38fe-82e7-1d185c260a82", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "bb61c905-4604-37c2-aa97-943041f6fef3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5790b1fb3d672d9a1fe3881a7181dfdbe741568f <1704aaaf5d22bc765c168402350d191e24e245bc"}, {"id": "c3a33cd3-b171-3e79-a2b5-edef9f8a380f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5790b1fb3d672d9a1fe3881a7181dfdbe741568f <5333e18e6b425fcc39c7fea89e3949a2a98bc5e4"}, {"id": "e8b25388-bbc7-3491-98d1-f6ab95a47780", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.7"}, {"id": "f6cc50a4-f3ad-35a1-97a4-3ad333154d83", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5790b1fb3d672d9a1fe3881a7181dfdbe741568f <c480f8af173d5b19c6d9c4311df6bbe352face9e"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2a974040-59f8-3e77-ad5f-4142dd7c7243", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}